{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjrGETWcvsBc71hYma25","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`node tools/test.mjs full` now passes on the final build: **1885 passed, 0 failed**. The HTML didn't change during that run (its hash still starts `7367bba6`), so the result applies to the file being handed in.\n\n## What changed since my last report\n- **Research field:** it now names my own reading (the hub README and client) and the plan stage's research, as section 19 asks. It's updated in the exit file and on the About screen, and the corrected text is below.\n- **Model field:** this stays at `reasoning effort medium`. Section 19 says to use TASK.md's wording, and \"max\" only appears in the plan's planning-stage report.\n- **Browser crash:** my first full rerun failed when the browser was killed mid-run, with only 2 GB of 19 GB free. That fits TASK.md's out-of-memory explanation, but I can't prove it was the cause. Every group then passed on its own, so I changed the test runner to start a fresh browser for each group, and `full` passed.\n\n## PLAN.md section 19 checklist, on the final file\n\n| Item | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Single HTML, opens from `file://`, no external requests, no audio files | `unit` and the audio test; a separate network check saw 0 requests |\n| WebGPU by default, WebGL2 fallback, ink filter, Rapier 0.19.3, Three R180 | `events` (all 14 events on WebGPU with the device alive, ink found in the pixels of one sampled frame, WebKit on WebGL2); `flow` checks versions |\n| Original cast, events, art and music; title from a real RNG | Name greps; title picked by `secrets.randbelow`, index 25 of 50; art judged by eye from screenshots |\n| All 13 events plus the finale, with tiers, intros, results and bots | `events`, `balance`, `ui`; nothing cut |\n| Programme to the ending, Wobble Age graph, jar, unlocks, Free Play | `flow` plays Day 1 through the ending into Day 6; the graph and unlock toast were not asserted directly, and I saw the graph in a screenshot |\n| Controller-first, keyboard and mouse, prompts follow the last device, Xbox glyphs | `input`, `ui` |\n| Attract at 10 s, Dev Mode from Pause with sliders and reset, touch-only message | `flow` (wall clock, each device exits), `ui` (Pixel 7, iPhone, iPad) |\n| Group Class 1–4; hub at 1, 2, 4 players, bad network, host leaving; game on its own | `input`, `hub` |\n| Music at 10%, all sound in code, every spoken word on screen | `audio`, `flow`; on-screen text comes from how speech is built, not a dedicated assertion |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | `unit` greps |\n| About, exit file and chat reply agree | `ui` checks About word for word against the exit file; the block below uses the same text |\n\n**Not checked, as TASK.md allows:** real controller, TV, phone and a human listener. Whether it's fun and whether the music is good are still unverified, and the skill numbers come from simulated bots.\n\n## Corrected report field\nEverything else in my previous report stands.\n\n- Research: Mine: the AI Hub session README and client. Beside this plan's, done at the planning stage and not repeated: the hub's protocol pages and code; background on the source from Wikipedia, a Nintendo World Report review and Nintendo's Iwata Asks interviews, read as search summaries\n\nNothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1000,"cache_read_input_tokens":523573,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1000},"output_tokens":743,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c3cb271-fa3a-4db7-9b9c-5b70edc7a0c6","uuid":"899ffbc0-5073-4f00-820e-10e648c40638","timestamp":"2026-11-05T13:21:02.357Z","request_id":"req_011CgjrGDop3