{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjsBmznZTBmGFVpkHF2y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`node tools/test.mjs full` passes on the final build: **2038 passed, 0 failed**. The hash of the HTML starts `a1efeefa`, and the last full run was on that file. The network check again saw no requests beyond the file itself.\n\n## Tests added\nYour hook was right that some items were only inferred, so I went back through plan sections 17 and 21 and added a `coverage` test group for them:\n\n| Item | Now checked by |\n|---|---|\n| Wobble Age graph | One point per age, lower age draws lower, the three numbers are correct |\n| Rest of the Journal | Calendar stamps, medal shelf, silly totals |\n| Unlocks | All six toast and save; The Mirror blocks locked hats |\n| Jar | Marbles are real physics balls, and they're counted and drawn |\n| Every word on screen | Eight speakers: the full line is typed out and matches the text the voice speaks; barks appear on screen too |\n| Animation | The mixer runs in all 14 events; Poses changes clips; ragdoll has 10 bodies and snaps back with no fall loop |\n| Live sliders | The real slider changes a running event; Reset to Defaults restores it |\n| Dev Mode | Every tool used with no errors; gust, fall, fruit, jumps and skips have their effects checked |\n| Group Class | Four pads play through to the podium; seats can leave; 4-to-1 points; the podium tips |\n| Other input and settings | Lost pad pauses and says so; audio-unlock tag; Plate Spinners' three key rates; Log Reps and Springboard on keys; Leave Class; difficulty; auto-breathe |\n\n## New bugs found\nThese two bring the total to 24 issues, 7 of them critical:\n- **Podium:** the top block slid sideways instead of tipping over. It now tips.\n- **Attract mode:** a key pressed in attract's very first frame was lost. This one was intermittent, so I ran the wall-clock test three more times after fixing it, and all passed.\n\n## Report changes\nThese replace the matching lines in my earlier report, and the exit file and About screen match:\n- **Testing Feedback 1:** 24 real issues, logged one line each in notes/issues.md as they happened.\n- **Testing field:** the group list now reads \"unit, flow, events, balance, input, coverage, audio, hub and ui groups\".\n\nEverything else in the report stands, including the Research line from my last message.\n\n## Still not verified\n- **Real hardware and people:** nobody has played this on a real controller, TV or phone, or listened to it. TASK.md says these aren't required.\n- **Fun and music:** whether the game is fun and whether the music is good can't be checked here; the bots only show the balance holds up in simulation.\n- **Plan details I simplified:**\n  - A hovered thing on the island gets a ring and a label, not the thick outline the plan describes.\n  - Stick and pointer steering are simulated by bots only in part: Plate Spinners on keys is checked for reaching the right speed bands, not for whether sharp bots still beat clumsy ones.\n\nNothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":416,"cache_read_input_tokens":542733,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":416},"output_tokens":728,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c3cb271-fa3a-4db7-9b9c-5b70edc7a0c6","uuid":"fa844027-a937-47ff-ad11-0962e836f2e7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T13:33:08.434Z","request_id":"req_011CgjsBmX2QXRNgMY1N9ECQ"}
