{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjuJrFxY6eScppzg2a11","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`node tools/test.mjs full` passes on the final file: **2171 passed, 0 failed** (the HTML's hash starts `b03d2b11`). It still makes no external requests. Every gap I listed last time is closed, except that I can't check real hardware or people from here. One balance question for you came out of this, below.\n\n## What I closed\n- **Trudy's faint:** she now faints at the ending. A new test also fails if any animation clip or sound effect is defined but never used.\n- **Group Class prompts:** each player's disc now lists every prompt for that event, on that player's own device. A test with pad and keyboard seats together confirms each keeps its own glyphs, stays inside the safe area and doesn't overlap the next seat.\n- **Bot evidence:**\n  - **Plate Spinners:** I removed the speed cap, slips and fudge factors I'd added, so the bot now uses only the plan's skill table. That showed a real game problem: the speed bands were too wide (1.00 / 1.00 / .89 share), so I narrowed them to 65%, adjustable by a new Dev Mode slider.\n  - **Keyboard bot:** it now also uses the plan's table, with one change: on keys it steers the ring and doesn't chase the dot, because the plan says that's what keyboard players do. I removed its Fruit Hat lean, gain and banking settings.\n\n## Balance on the final build\n| Event | Sharp | Average | Clumsy |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Plate Spinners, stick (form) | 100 | 87 | 60 |\n| Plate Spinners, keys (share alive) | .97 | .90 | .71 |\n| Step Class, keys (form) | 94 | 83 | 68 |\n| Fruit Hat, keys (form) | 75 | 74 | 68 |\n\n## Decision for you\nShould parking and breathing be able to earn top marks in Poses? If you leave the stick on the target and breathe in time, you get top marks on the first two tiers.\n\n| Poses, parked on target | Gentle | Honest | Unreasonable |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| With breath in sync | 100 | 100 | 69 |\n| Without breath | 80 | 54 | 34 |\n\nThe plan's own guard only covers parking without breath, and its bot figures also reach 100 with breath, so I left this as it is. Breathing in time is a real skill, but this makes the easier tiers quite forgiving. To tighten it, lower the breath bonus; that's a small change, but it moves away from the plan's numbers.\n\n## Report changes\n- **Testing Feedback 1:** 28 real issues, logged one line each in notes/issues.md as they happened. The 28th is the Plate Spinners bands. The critical count stays at 9, and the exit file and About screen match.\n\n## Still not checked\n- **Real hardware and people:** nobody has used a real controller, TV or phone, or listened to it. TASK.md says these aren't required.\n- **Fun and music:** whether it's fun and whether the music is good are still open. The bots show the balance holds up in simulation, but their error sizes are the plan's assumptions.\n- **Mouse skill:** mouse play is tested for input, not simulated for skill, which the plan accepts.\n\nNothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1528,"cache_read_input_tokens":594027,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1528},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c3cb271-fa3a-4db7-9b9c-5b70edc7a0c6","uuid":"5611483c-53ea-4bad-83e8-2a8d278bb78a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:00:59.719Z","request_id":"req_011CgjuJqeFKNQGom74Ru4Yu"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.]: The final message itself leaves an open decision: it asks the user whether parked-and-breathing should earn top marks in Poses, and it says the current tuning lets it reach 100 on the first two tiers, against the plan's intent. It also says the 'Decision for you' is unresolved and that the plan's bot figures and the implemented breath bonus were left as they are. The message also states that real hardware, people and fun/music checks are unverified, which the plan does not list as 'never required' for every item, though TASK.md allows them to be left. Transcript evidence therefore shows at least one PLAN.md balance question not reconciled with the plan, so 'everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done' is not evidenced."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c3cb271-fa3a-4db7-9b9c-5b70edc7a0c6","uuid":"3947d7fc-493a-4402-9bb7-5ce09a26a28c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:01:02.249Z","isSynthetic":true}
