{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjumSetCbcVmj8k6b5vQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`node tools/test.mjs full` passes on the final file: **2177 passed, 0 failed** (the HTML's hash starts `3afc282e`), and it still makes no external requests. The Poses question is settled and no decision is left with you.\n\n## Poses: parking no longer earns Exemplary\nPLAN.md says to decide where it's silent, so I did. Holding still should mean correcting by hand, and that's the plan's own reason for having sway. Poses now adds a slow drift during holds, which a parked stick can't follow but a player watching the dot can. It's a new tuning value on top of the plan's numbers, and breathing in time still reduces it. The breath bonus itself is unchanged.\n\n| Poses form | Gentle | Honest | Unreasonable |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Parked, breathing in time (before) | 100 | 100 | 69 |\n| Parked, breathing in time (now, range over 4 seeds) | 68–84 | 64–80 | 56–59 |\n| Parked, no breath (now, range over 4 seeds) | 39–44 | 35–41 | 30–32 |\n| Correcting and breathing: sharp / average / clumsy | 100 / 100 / 95 | 100 / 94 / 85 | 95 / 86 / 73 |\n| Correcting, no breath: sharp / average / clumsy | 68 / 55 / 47 | 60 / 47 / 45 | 53 / 42 / 40 |\n\nA new permanent test fails if parked play reaches Exemplary (85) on any tier. This does differ from the plan's bot figures in places: correcting without breath is now harder (sharp 68 against the plan's 95 on Gentle), while average and clumsy bots score higher than the plan's when breathing. That fits the plan's \"breath is how you get there\", but those figures aren't the plan's numbers any more.\n\n## Report change\n- **Testing Feedback 1:** 29 real issues, logged one line each in notes/issues.md as they happened. The critical count stays at 9, and the exit file and About screen match.\n\n## Hand-in, all in `work/`\n- `TotterFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-045333.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `TotterFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-045333/` (dev folder)\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n\n## Limits of this computer\nTASK.md says checks that need the real thing are \"never required\", and these are the only ones left: a real controller, TV or phone, and a person playing or listening. So whether it's fun and whether the music is good are still unjudged. The audio is checked only as signals, and the skill numbers come from simulated bots.\n\nNothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1565,"cache_read_input_tokens":600208,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1565},"output_tokens":822,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c3cb271-fa3a-4db7-9b9c-5b70edc7a0c6","uuid":"f3f11b54-0dd7-4408-9e98-436929ecbf22","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:06:56.480Z","request_id":"req_011CgjumSHoMHnJoNRfZmRjC"}
