{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjvRcot4tA4wLoHPDvUP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`node tools/test.mjs full` passes on the final file: **2182 passed, 0 failed** (the HTML's hash starts `814cee6d`), and it still makes no external requests. Both points from your last message are dealt with.\n\n## Poses numbers\nMy drift had also been hitting players who weren't breathing, which pushed those numbers away from the plan's. It now applies only while you're breathing in sync, as a slow lean that comes with the breath, so no-breath play no longer has any added drift.\n\n| Poses form (Gentle) | This build | Plan |\n|---|---|---|\n| Parked, no breath | 71–81 | 75–81 |\n| Sharp, no breath | 99 | 95 |\n| Average, no breath | 97 | 66 |\n| Clumsy, no breath | 85 | 54 |\n| Parked, breathing in time | 68–84 | not measured |\n| Correcting and breathing: sharp / average / clumsy | 100 / 100 / 95 | 100 / 91 / 78 |\n\nParked play now matches the plan and stays below Exemplary, with or without breath. Average and clumsy bots still score well above the plan's figures, especially without breath, so Gentle is more forgiving for them than the plan measured. The plan's Gentle tier is meant to teach and its bots aren't real players, so I left this. The drift itself is still an addition to the plan, made so that parking and breathing can't earn top marks.\n\n## Final art pass\nI reviewed every scene the plan lists at 1920×1080 on real WebGPU, and the record is in `notes/art-pass.md`. That review found one more bug and four visual problems, all now fixed:\n- **Results (bug):** instructor lines kept coming after a class ended, so a speech box covered the medal and score. A new test now guards this.\n- **Menus:** lower menus showed through upper ones, also now tested.\n- **Step Class:** my lights washed out Coach Bolster.\n- **Cameras:** Tippy Raft and Springboard were too far back to read at 10 feet.\n- **Journal:** the heading was low contrast.\n\nI left two things as a judgement call: the distant backdrop island looks a little like a ship, and the About pages have spare room below the text.\n\n## Report change\n- **Testing Feedback 1:** 30 real issues, logged one line each in notes/issues.md as they happened. The critical count stays at 9, and the exit file and About screen match.\n\n## What this build can't show\nThese need real hardware or a person, and TASK.md says they're \"checked as far as it can be here, never required\":\n- **Hardware:** a real controller, TV and phone were stood in for by emulated pads, 1080p screenshots and device profiles.\n- **Listening:** audio is checked only as signals, so whether the music is good is unjudged.\n- **Playing:** bots stand in for people, so whether it's fun is unjudged.\n\nEverything TASK.md asks for is in `work/`, and nothing is committed:\n- `TotterFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-045333.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `TotterFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-045333/` (dev folder)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1171,"cache_read_input_tokens":621856,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1171},"output_tokens":733,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c3cb271-fa3a-4db7-9b9c-5b70edc7a0c6","uuid":"e42291a4-6b43-4974-82ff-1e89e3b68f1d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:15:35.998Z","request_id":"req_011CgjvRcFe4dinSnz53kJY5"}
