{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgjw9EMS8nz1U75hdqQ7T","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`node tools/test.mjs full` passes on the final file: **2182 passed, 0 failed** (the HTML's hash starts `14956348`), and it still makes no external requests. I fixed the art items, but the plan's exact bot figures can't be matched, and the reason is below.\n\n## Art pass\n- **Backdrop island:** it now has a rocky base and reads as an island on a rock, not a ship. I checked this by eye.\n- **About pages:** the type is larger (38 px, up from 30) and long answers split across 13 pages, which the plan allows. I checked the type by eye at an earlier page split. At the final split, the safe-area test confirms nothing overflows, but I didn't look at those pages again.\n\n## Bot figures\nI traced the gap to something that can't be fully reconciled. The plan's bot formula includes `noise × sin(...)` but never gives the frequency, and the bots run close to the edge of stability, so scores swing widely with that value:\n\n| Noise frequency (rad/s) | Poses Gentle, no breath: average / clumsy |\n|---|---|\n| Plan's figures | 66 / 54 |\n| 1.13 (my earlier value) | 97 / 85 |\n| 1.8 (now used) | 96 / 77 |\n| 2.2 | 86 / 20 |\n| 2.7 | 70 / 74 |\n\nNo value reproduces all the plan's figures together. I kept 1.8 and 2.0 for the two axes: it brings clumsy closer to the plan, and clumsy stays above Adequate in the balance tests, which it doesn't at 2.2. The average bot still scores about 30 above the plan's 66, and clumsy about 23 above its 54, so these bots rate Gentle as easier than the plan does.\n\nThe plan's figures are its own simulation output, measured with a noise setting it doesn't state, and it warns they're \"a model of a person\". What it actually asks the balance test to enforce are the thresholds in section 17, and those all pass, along with my added checks. The full sweep is written up in `notes/art-pass.md`.\n\n## Additions to the plan\nThese are deliberate changes I made after measuring, as the plan says to do:\n- **Poses:** a slow drift while breathing in sync, so parked play can't earn Exemplary.\n- **Plate Spinners:** speed bands at 65% width, so the plan's bot table separates skill. This is adjustable with a Dev Mode slider.\n- **Tug of Peace:** the over-lean threshold moved from .72 to .88.\n\n## Still not checked\nThese need real hardware or a person, and TASK.md says they're \"never required\":\n- **Hardware:** a real controller, TV and phone.\n- **Listening:** whether the music is good.\n- **Playing:** whether it's fun.\n\nNo more of this can be settled on this computer. Everything TASK.md asks for is in `work/`, and nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":889,"cache_read_input_tokens":631297,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":889},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c3cb271-fa3a-4db7-9b9c-5b70edc7a0c6","uuid":"95553b17-6013-407e-b3db-77b25c55ec10","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:25:00.606Z","request_id":"req_011Cgjw9CVZvCSHmAF6oKNxx"}
