{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjwSJaezfcnnRboEwcnE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The plan's .72 works now that the bot is fixed, so my retune was only masking a bot bug, and I'm restoring the plan's number. I'll add a permanent test for that behaviour and correct the exit file's \"What was confusing\" answer, which wrongly blamed the plan.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2523,"cache_read_input_tokens":644589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2523},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c3cb271-fa3a-4db7-9b9c-5b70edc7a0c6","uuid":"48226aac-8808-4dba-a425-56a824c54100","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:28:53.847Z","request_id":"req_011CgjwSJ1g8kEwMbJZN11rq","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":2,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjwSJaezfcnnRboEwcnE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EkALrvAwpywME5YbdKRDgq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"rm -f notes/tugsweep.js; python3 -I - <<'E'\ndef sub(path, old, new):\n    s=open(path).read(); assert old in s, (path, old[:60]); open(path,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nsub('src/events/tug.js',\"const stick = this.tier.ease ? (this.tierIndex === 2 ? .95 : .85) : .9;\",\"const stick = this.tier.ease ? .85 : .9;\")\nsub('../exit-interview.json',\"In my build the plan's Tug of Peace over-lean figure (.72) didn't produce its own results table, and I retuned it to .88. Also SOURCE\",\"The plan's bot model doesn't state its noise frequency, and bot scores swing widely with it, so its skill figures can't be reproduced exactly; I chose the closest stable value. Also SOURCE\")\nsub('../exit-interview.json',\"30 real issues, logged\",\"32 real issues, logged\")\nsub('../exit-interview.json','\"9: a crash in The Cairn','\"10: a crash in The Cairn')\nsub('../exit-interview.json',\"quick foot taps not counting on a keyboard; and presses lost during a hit-stop.\",\"quick foot taps not counting on a keyboard; presses lost during a hit-stop; and Tug of Peace losing its one decision, because a retune of mine had hidden a bot bug.\")\ns=open('test/balance.mjs').read()\nmarker=\"  const tg = await run('tug', 'average');\"\nadd=r\"\"\"  // Tug of Peace: how far to lean is the game. A stick at .85 is safe and wins; full stick sits you down.\n  const TUG = (tier, skill, stick) => page.evaluate(([t, s, st]) => { const E = __TEST__.EVENTS.tug.prototype, orig = E.botInput; E.botInput = function (i, tt, sk, dt) { const r = orig.call(this, i, tt, sk, dt), l = this.lanes[i]; const [x, z] = l.brain.correct(dt, l, 0, st, false, .5); return { ...r, x, z }; }; __TEST__.seed(29); const R = __TEST__.runEvent('tug', { tier: t, skills: [s] }); E.botInput = orig; const p = R.res[0].big.split('-').map(Number); return { won: p[0] > p[1], falls: R.res[0].falls }; }, [tier, skill, stick]);\n  for (const tier of [1, 2]) for (const s of SK) { const safe = await TUG(tier, s, .85); T.ok(safe.won && safe.falls <= 1, `tug T${tier + 1} ${s} at .85 should be safe and win: ${JSON.stringify(safe)}`); }\n  for (const tier of [1, 2]) { const greedy = await TUG(tier, 'sharp', 1); T.ok(greedy.falls >= 3, `tug T${tier + 1} full stick should sit you down: ${JSON.stringify(greedy)}`); }\n  for (const [tier, want] of [[0, [100, 89, 82]], [1, [89, 86, 74]], [2, [79, 76, 66]]]) { const got = []; for (const s of SK) { let v = 0; for (let d = 1; d <= 3; d++) { v += (await run('plates', s, {}, tier, d * 37)).res[0].raw; } got.push(v / 3 * 100); } got.forEach((g, i) => T.ok(Math.abs(g - want[i]) <= 10, `plates T${tier + 1} ${SK[i]} share ${g.toFixed(0)}, plan ${want[i]}`)); }\n\"\"\"\nassert marker in s; s=s.replace(marker,add+marker); open('test/balance.mjs','w').write(s)\ns=open('notes/art-pass.md').read()\ns+=\"\"\"\n# About at the final pagination\nAll 13 pages reviewed by eye at 1920x1080: nothing clipped, each page readable. Fixed a stray colon after questions.\n\n# Numbers against the plan, on the final build\nRestored the plan's value: Tug over-lean .72 (a retune to .88 had been hiding a bot bug).\nChanged after measuring, as the plan says to: Plate Spinners bands at 65% width (share T1 100/93/80, plan 100/89/82; T2 98/88/75, plan 89/86/74; T3 86/80/68, plan 79/76/66). Poses gains a slow lean only while breathing in sync, so parked play stays below Exemplary.\nTug at .72: T1 at .9 everyone wins in 23-32 s (plan 25-48). T2 and T3 at .85 everyone wins with almost no falls (plan: T3 sharp only). Full stick falls about 9-16 times a class on T2 and 6-9 on T3 (plan 3-4 and 6-7), so greed costs more than the plan measured. T3 at .95 falls too (plan: mostly wins).\n\"\"\"\nopen('notes/art-pass.md','w').write(s)\nE\nrm -rf notes/shots; node tools/build.mjs | tail -1; timeout 200 node tools/test.mjs balance 2>&1 | grep -E '^FAIL|passed|crashed' | cut -c1-200","description":"Restore plan value, add outcome tests, fix the exit answer","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2523,"cache_read_input_tokens":644589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2523},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c3cb271-fa3a-4db7-9b9c-5b70edc7a0c6","uuid":"1c44eaa3-4f60-4fd4-b939-b3f7eb056e82","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:29:07.271Z","request_id":"req_011CgjwSJ1g8kEwMbJZN11rq","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EkALrvAwpywME5YbdKRDgq":{"command":"rm -f notes/tugsweep.js; python3 -I - <<'E'\ndef sub(path, old, new):\n    s=open(path).read(); assert old in s, (path, old[:60]); open(path,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nsub('src/events/tug.js',\"const stick = this.tier.ease ? (this.tierIndex === 2 ? .95 : .85) : .9;\",\"const stick = this.tier.ease ? .85 : .9;\")\nsub('../exit-interview.json',\"In my build the plan's Tug of Peace over-lean figure (.72) didn't produce its own results table, and I retuned it to .88. Also SOURCE\",\"The plan's bot model doesn't state its noise frequency, and bot scores swing widely with it, so its skill figures can't be reproduced exactly; I chose the closest stable value. Also SOURCE\")\nsub('../exit-interview.json',\"30 real issues, logged\",\"32 real issues, logged\")\nsub('../exit-interview.json','\"9: a crash in The Cairn','\"10: a crash in The Cairn')\nsub('../exit-interview.json',\"quick foot taps not counting on a keyboard; and presses lost during a hit-stop.\",\"quick foot taps not counting on a keyboard; presses lost during a hit-stop; and Tug of Peace losing its one decision, because a retune of mine had hidden a bot bug.\")\ns=open('test/balance.mjs').read()\nmarker=\"  const tg = await run('tug', 'average');\"\nadd=r\"\"\"  // Tug of Peace: how far to lean is the game. A stick at .85 is safe and wins; full stick sits you down.\n  const TUG = (tier, skill, stick) => page.evaluate(([t, s, st]) => { const E = __TEST__.EVENTS.tug.prototype, orig = E.botInput; E.botInput = function (i, tt, sk, dt) { const r = orig.call(this, i, tt, sk, dt), l = this.lanes[i]; const [x, z] = l.brain.correct(dt, l, 0, st, false, .5); return { ...r, x, z }; }; __TEST__.seed(29); const R = __TEST__.runEvent('tug', { tier: t, skills: [s] }); E.botInput = orig; const p = R.res[0].big.split('-').map(Number); return { won: p[0] > p[1], falls: R.res[0].falls }; }, [tier, skill, stick]);\n  for (const tier of [1, 2]) for (const s of SK) { const safe = await TUG(tier, s, .85); T.ok(safe.won && safe.falls <= 1, `tug T${tier + 1} ${s} at .85 should be safe and win: ${JSON.stringify(safe)}`); }\n  for (const tier of [1, 2]) { const greedy = await TUG(tier, 'sharp', 1); T.ok(greedy.falls >= 3, `tug T${tier + 1} full stick should sit you down: ${JSON.stringify(greedy)}`); }\n  for (const [tier, want] of [[0, [100, 89, 82]], [1, [89, 86, 74]], [2, [79, 76, 66]]]) { const got = []; for (const s of SK) { let v = 0; for (let d = 1; d <= 3; d++) { v += (await run('plates', s, {}, tier, d * 37)).res[0].raw; } got.push(v / 3 * 100); } got.forEach((g, i) => T.ok(Math.abs(g - want[i]) <= 10, `plates T${tier + 1} ${SK[i]} share ${g.toFixed(0)}, plan ${want[i]}`)); }\n\"\"\"\nassert marker in s; s=s.replace(marker,add+marker); open('test/balance.mjs','w').write(s)\ns=open('notes/art-pass.md').read()\ns+=\"\"\"\n# About at the final pagination\nAll 13 pages reviewed by eye at 1920x1080: nothing clipped, each page readable. Fixed a stray colon after questions.\n\n# Numbers against the plan, on the final build\nRestored the plan's value: Tug over-lean .72 (a retune to .88 had been hiding a bot bug).\nChanged after measuring, as the plan says to: Plate Spinners bands at 65% width (share T1 100/93/80, plan 100/89/82; T2 98/88/75, plan 89/86/74; T3 86/80/68, plan 79/76/66). Poses gains a slow lean only while breathing in sync, so parked play stays below Exemplary.\nTug at .72: T1 at .9 everyone wins in 23-32 s (plan 25-48). T2 and T3 at .85 everyone wins with almost no falls (plan: T3 sharp only). Full stick falls about 9-16 times a class on T2 and 6-9 on T3 (plan 3-4 and 6-7), so greed costs more than the plan measured. T3 at .95 falls too (plan: mostly wins).\n\"\"\"\nopen('notes/art-pass.md','w').write(s)\nE\nrm -rf notes/shots; node tools/build.mjs | tail -1; timeout 200 node tools/test.mjs balance 2>&1 | grep -E '^FAIL|passed|crashed' | cut -c1-200","description":"Restore plan value, add outcome tests, fix the exit answer","timeout":300000}}}
