{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjwvhrfzMzb5VESG7MsH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game and hand-in files are unchanged since the last full run: **2200 passed, 0 failed** on the final file (hash `75a0bb40`). This round added only a note in `notes/art-pass.md`. I'm stopping the tuning here, because the remaining differences from the plan can't be closed honestly, and more retuning would only make the numbers look better.\n\n## Why the remaining differences stay\n\n**Tug of Peace's table can't be fully reached under the plan's own rules.** The plan wants a stick at .95 to be safe on the top tier while full stick falls, but the two produce almost the same lean, because the ankle's torque limit saturates:\n\n| Stick (Unreasonable) | Average lean share |\n|---|---|\n| .85 | .69–.73 |\n| .95 | .76–.79 |\n| Full | .78–.80 |\n\nNo threshold can make .95 safe and full stick fall. I kept the plan's .72, which makes .85 safe and anything above it risky, so the event's decision is intact.\n\n**Poses bot figures depend on a value the plan doesn't state.** The noise frequency isn't given, and scores swing widely with it (average 97, 96, 86 and 70 across the values I tried). The only ways to force a match are giving each bot its own value or retuning the game to suit the bots. Either would make the table match while showing nothing about the game, so I won't do it.\n\n**The plan treats these figures as measurements, not targets.**\n- It calls its skill results \"simulations of a player, not a player\" and says the bots are \"a model of a person\".\n- It tells the builder to \"tune it\" and to \"measure before you trust a number\", and warns that building will overturn numbers as it did for the planner.\n- What it asks the balance test to enforce are section 17's thresholds, and those all pass.\n\n## Differences you may want to look at\nThese are all my choices, so they're open to you to overrule:\n- **Poses:** a slow lean while breathing in sync, so parked play can't earn Exemplary.\n- **Plate Spinners:** speed bands at 65% width, adjustable with a Dev Mode slider. Results land close to the plan's on all three tiers.\n- **Bot noise frequency:** 1.8 and 2.0 rad/s for the two axes, the closest stable fit.\n- **Tug of Peace:** greed costs more falls than the plan measured, and .85 wins for everyone on the upper tiers.\n- **Poses bots:** the average and clumsy bots score above the plan's figures on Gentle, so it may be more forgiving than the plan intended.\n\n## If your stop condition needs these figures matched\nI can't meet that reading of it, and it needs your decision, not more work from me. If the plan's table is what you want, the Tug rules themselves would have to change, for example the torque limit or how share is measured. That's a design change I wouldn't make on my own.\n\n## Where things stand\nEverything else in PLAN.md that can be done here is done, including the art pass recorded in `notes/art-pass.md`. A real controller, TV and phone, and a person listening and playing, remain unchecked; TASK.md says those are \"never required\". So whether the game is fun and whether the music is good are still unjudged. Everything TASK.md asks for is in `work/`, and nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":685,"cache_read_input_tokens":654568,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":685},"output_tokens":689,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c3cb271-fa3a-4db7-9b9c-5b70edc7a0c6","uuid":"c499c579-ea42-44d1-a220-4b3c718c74be","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:35:18.003Z","request_id":"req_011CgjwvhQP2E8xpGdgCSHzP"}
